'\" t
.nh
.TH ysd 1 "" YAMLSchema YAMLSchema
\fBysd\fR converts between \fB\&.ysd\fR, canonical \fB\&.ysdc\fR, and JSON Schema.
It reads standard input when no input path is given and writes to standard
output unless \fB-o\fR names a file.

.PP
See the
installation instructions
\[la]https://yamlschema.org/getting\-started/#install\-the\-command\[ra]\&.

.SH Usage
.EX
ysd --help
ysd [INPUT]
ysd (-t FORMAT | -o FILE) [INPUT]
ysd -N, --norm [INPUT]
ysd -R, --roundtrip [-q, --quiet] [INPUT]
.EE

.SH Options
.TS
allbox;
l l
l l .
\fBOption\fP	\fBMeaning\fP
\fB-t\fR, \fB--to FORMAT\fR	Select \fBysd\fR, \fBysdc\fR, or \fBjsc\fR
\fB-f\fR, \fB--from FORMAT\fR	Select \fBysd\fR, \fBysdc\fR, or \fBjsc\fR input
\fB-Y\fR, \fB--yaml\fR	Emit YAML output
\fB-J\fR, \fB--json\fR	Emit JSON output
\fB-o\fR, \fB--output FILE\fR	Write to a file, or use \fB-\fR for standard output
\fB-N\fR, \fB--norm\fR	T{
Normalize to draft 2020-12 JSON Schema
T}
\fB-R\fR, \fB--roundtrip\fR	T{
Test a JSON Schema or .ysd roundtrip
T}
\fB-q\fR, \fB--quiet\fR	T{
Suppress successful roundtrip output
T}
\fB-C\fR, \fB--compact\fR	Emit compact JSON
\fB--help\fR	Show command help
\fB--version\fR	Show the installed version
.TE

.SH Shell completion
The sourced installer enables completion automatically in Bash, Zsh, and
Fish by sourcing the matching script from the installed repository.
The scripts can also be sourced directly from a checkout or installation:

.EX
source /path/to/yamlschema/share/complete.bash
source /path/to/yamlschema/share/complete.zsh
.EE

.EX
source /path/to/yamlschema/share/complete.fish
.EE

.PP
The installed \fB\&.rc\fR also adds the bundled manuals to \fBMANPATH\fR\&.
Use \fBman ysd\fR, \fBman yamlschema\fR, \fBman yamlschema-design\fR, or
\fBman yamlschema-json-schema\fR\&.

.SH Default direction
The first non-whitespace character and the filename extension determine the
input form.
JSON input converts to .ysd, while .ysd and .ysdc input convert to JSON Schema.

.PP
The recognized filename extensions are \fB\&.ysd.yaml\fR, \fB\&.ysd.json\fR,
\fB\&.ysdc.yaml\fR, \fB\&.ysdc.json\fR, \fB\&.schema.json\fR, \fB\&.schema.json.yaml\fR,
\fB\&.schema.yaml\fR, and \fB\&.schema.yml\fR\&.

.EX
ysd contact.schema.json
ysd contact.ysd.yaml
ysd contact.ysdc.yaml
ysd contact.ysdc.json
.EE

.PP
Use \fB-f\fR when reading standard input or when a filename is ambiguous:

.EX
cat contact.yaml | ysd -f ysd -t jsc
.EE

.SH Explicit targets
The \fB\&.ysd\fR and \fB\&.ysdc\fR targets emit YAML by default, while \fBjsc\fR emits JSON.
Use \fB-Y\fR / \fB--yaml\fR or \fB-J\fR / \fB--json\fR to override that default.
The output options and a recognized output filename extension must agree.

.EX
ysd -t ysd contact.schema.json
ysd -t ysdc contact.ysd.yaml
ysd -t ysdc -J contact.ysd.yaml
ysd -t jsc contact.ysd.yaml
ysd -t jsc -Y contact.ysd.yaml
.EE

.SH Normalize JSON Schema
Normalization adds the draft 2020-12 dialect, chooses canonical keyword
positions, and preserves property order.

.EX
ysd -N contact.schema.json
ysd -N -Y contact.schema.json
.EE

.PP
\fB-C\fR / \fB--compact\fR applies only to JSON output.

.SH Roundtrip reports
Roundtrip checks begin from the input representation:

.EX
ysd -R contact.schema.json
ysd -R contact.ysd.yaml
.EE

.PP
Use quiet mode in automation:

.EX
ysd -Rq contact.ysd.yaml
.EE

.PP
A successful quiet check produces no output and exits successfully.
